      "level": 5,
      "node_type": "section",
      "title": "Section",
      "text": "Short title and commencement. (1) This Act may be called the Indian Contract Act, 1892. (2) It shall come into force on the first day of July, 1892.",
      "start_page": 1,
      "end_page": 1,
      "numbering": "1",
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "node_id": "n_0003",
      "parent_id": "n_0001",
      "level": 5,
      "node_type": "section",
      "title": "Section",
      "text": "Definitions.\nIn this Act, unless there is anything repugnant in the subject or context, (a) \"contract\" means an agreement enforceable by law; (b) \"promise\" means a proposal accepted. (i) where the proposal is made (ii) where the acceptance is communicated\nExplanation.—Nothing in this section shall apply to\nIllustration.—A says to B\nProviso.—Provided that",
      "start_page": 1,
      "end_page": 1,
      "numbering": "2",
      "children": []
    },
